---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Terms and Conditions of Sale
permalink: /conditions-of-sale/
---
{# Conditions of Sale (Figma 35098:39725, the client's 1600px frame on the WIP page); the URL is the live site's.
   No redesigned or phone frame exists, so the page uses the redesign's components and type scale, as the repair
   pages do. The frame draws sections 1, 2 and 4.7; the rest of the text is the live page's (src/_data/conditionsOfSale.js).
   - Hero: the shared content hero with the frame's photo, fade, title and intro, and the live page's effective date.
   - Section bar ("Contents Sub Menu" 35098:39780): the frame's #f5f8fa bar and seven links, sticky under the header
     like the About sub-nav. The link of the section in view is orange (the frame's orange "Warranty" is that state).
     Phones scroll the links sideways.
   - "Search Terms & Conditions" (35098:39790), in the PLP's "Search within" field, works: it keeps only the
     subsections that mention the words and marks them (termsSearch in content.js).
   - Sections: the frame's title with a rule to its right, white and #f5f8fa in turn (as Section 1 and 2). The frame's
     "Back to Top" under each section is one sticky button instead. The text keeps the 756px reading width; from xl the room to its right holds
     the section's subsection index, sticky under the bar (the frame's hidden rows 35098:39900 to 40038 list the
     same subsections, with the live page's shorter titles).
   - Tables (4.5, and 4.7 with all 45 product lines) look like the repair price tables; the 4.7 table keeps the
     frame's search field (the same PLP field), which filters its product lines.
   - "Questions About These Terms?": the live page's closing contact box, as a tinted callout. #}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{% import "content/macros.njk" as c with context %}
{% set t = conditionsOfSale %}
{# The section bar is 57px tall on phones and 69px from md (with its border); sections start under it and
   subsections 24px lower. #}
{% set sectionOffset = "scroll-mt-[57px] md:scroll-mt-[69px]" %}
{% set itemOffset = "scroll-mt-[81px] md:scroll-mt-[93px]" %}

{# Search field: the PLP's "Search within" field (plp/macros.njk, 34723:17182) instead of the frame's input with the
   orange button: 320px from md, the navy search icon inside on the left, filtering as you type.
   model: the Alpine property it edits; submit: Alpine expression on Enter. #}
{% macro searchField(placeholder, label, model, submit) %}
<form role="search" @submit.prevent="{{ submit }}" class="w-full md:w-[320px]">
  <label class="relative block">
    <span class="sr-only">{{ label }}</span>
    <span class="pointer-events-none absolute left-5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2 text-primary-500">{% icon "search" %}</span>
    <input type="search" enterkeyhint="search" autocomplete="off" x-model.debounce.150ms="{{ model }}" @keydown.escape="{{ model }} = ''" placeholder="{{ placeholder }}" class="input pl-[60px] font-medium placeholder:font-medium">
  </label>
</form>
{% endmacro %}

{# Table in the repair price tables' look (Micro Instrument Repair): navy header (SemiBold, white), rows white and
   #f5f8fa in turn with the 1px outline lines, 4px corners, "Not Returnable" in Bold. The first column takes the rest
   of the width. Phones: 14/20 text, 104px value columns. tb.filter: rows rendered by Alpine (tableFilter) under
   the search field; the empty row says when no product line matches. #}
{% macro table(tb) %}
{% set head = "bg-primary-500 px-3 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white md:px-4 md:py-4 md:text-lg" %}
{% set cell = "border-b border-l border-outline px-3 pb-[11px] pt-3 md:px-4 md:py-3" %}
<table class="w-full table-fixed border-separate border-spacing-0 text-left">
  <colgroup><col>{% for h in tb.head %}{% if not loop.first %}<col class="w-[104px] md:w-[200px]">{% endif %}{% endfor %}</colgroup>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      {% for h in tb.head %}
      <th scope="col" class="{{ head }} {{ 'rounded-tl' if loop.first }} {{ 'rounded-tr' if loop.last else 'border-r border-white/30' }}">{{ h }}</th>
      {% endfor %}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody class="text-sm text-primary-500 md:text-lg">
    {% if tb.filter %}
    <template x-for="(row, i) in shown" :key="row[0]">
      <tr>
        <th scope="row" x-text="row[0]" class="{{ cell }} font-normal" :class="{ 'bg-menu': i % 2, 'bg-white': !(i % 2), 'rounded-bl': i === shown.length - 1 }"></th>
        <template x-for="(v, j) in row.slice(1)" :key="j">
          <td x-text="v" class="{{ cell }}" :class="{ 'bg-menu': i % 2, 'bg-white': !(i % 2), 'font-bold': v === 'Not Returnable', 'border-r': j === row.length - 2, 'rounded-br': j === row.length - 2 && i === shown.length - 1 }"></td>
        </template>
      </tr>
    </template>
    <tr x-show="!shown.length" x-cloak>
      <td colspan="{{ tb.head | length }}" class="{{ cell }} rounded-b border-r bg-white text-body">No product line matches “<span x-text="q.trim()"></span>”.</td>
    </tr>
    {% else %}
    {% for row in tb.rows %}
    {% set tint = "bg-menu" if loop.index % 2 == 0 else "bg-white" %}
    {% set lastRow = loop.last %}
    <tr>
      {% for v in row %}
      {% if loop.first %}
      <th scope="row" class="{{ cell }} {{ tint }} {{ 'rounded-bl' if lastRow }} font-normal">{{ v }}</th>
      {% else %}
      <td class="{{ cell }} {{ tint }} {{ 'border-r' if loop.last }} {{ 'rounded-br' if lastRow and loop.last }} {{ 'font-bold' if v == 'Not Returnable' }}">{{ v }}</td>
      {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table>
{% endmacro %}

{# One block of a subsection (see src/_data/conditionsOfSale.js). Bullets are the redesign's orange dashes
   (About 34974:1180) instead of the frame's dots; the notice box is the frame's "Disclaimer" (35098:39802) with the
   outline border of the tinted callouts, white on the #f5f8fa sections. #}
{% macro block(b, tinted) %}
{% if b.h %}
<h4 class="mt-2 text-lg font-bold text-heading md:text-h4">{{ b.h }}</h4>
{% elif b.note %}
<p class="rounded border border-outline {{ 'bg-white' if tinted else 'bg-menu' }} px-5 py-4 md:px-6" data-figma="35098:39802">{{ b.note }}</p>
{% elif b.list %}
<ul class="flex flex-col gap-1">
  {% for li in b.list %}
  <li class="flex gap-3"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-[11px] h-0.5 w-2 shrink-0 rounded-[1px] bg-accent md:mt-[13px]"></span><span class="min-w-0">{{ li | safe }}</span></li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
{% elif b.ordered %}
<ol class="flex list-decimal flex-col gap-1 pl-6 marker:font-medium">
  {% for li in b.ordered %}<li class="pl-1">{{ li | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ol>
{% elif b.table and b.table.filter %}
<div x-data="tableFilter({{ b.table.rows | json }})" class="flex flex-col gap-4 md:gap-6" data-figma="35098:39840">
  <div class="flex justify-end" data-figma="35098:39836">{{ searchField("Search product lines", "Search the product lines in the table", "q", "") }}</div>
  {{ table(b.table) }}
</div>
{% elif b.table %}
{{ table(b.table) }}
{% elif b.footnote %}
<p class="flex gap-2 text-sm text-body md:text-base"><span class="w-5 shrink-0 font-bold text-primary-500">{{ b.footnote }}</span><span>{{ b.p | safe }}</span></p>
{% else %}
<p>{{ b.p | safe }}</p>
{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}

{{ ui.breadcrumbs([{ label: "Terms and Conditions" }]) }}

{# Hero: the hand signing a document on the right under the frame's fade (termsFade). From lg the photo is 1136x640
   (Figma's 144% x 129% fill of its 682x429 box, cropped from the top-left as there) starting where the frame has it
   (57.5% at 1600, 50% + 120px beside the centred content, never over the 625px text column) and reaching the right
   edge on wide screens. Phones and tablets have no room beside the long intro: the photo covers the hero with the hand
   on the right, under the phone fade and a 60% navy tint that keeps the white text readable over the paper. #}
{% call c.hero({
  title: t.title, text: t.intro, figma: "35098:39773", image: "344359dd",
  fade: contentPages.gradients.termsFade, fadeAt: "lg",
  photo: "inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-[55%_center] lg:inset-auto lg:left-[max(625px,calc(50%_+_120px))] lg:top-0 lg:h-[max(640px,100%)] lg:w-[max(1136px,calc(50%_-_120px))] lg:max-w-none lg:object-left-top",
  scrim: "bg-primary-500/60 lg:hidden"
}) %}
  <p class="text-sm text-white md:text-base"><span class="font-medium">Effective Date:</span> {{ t.effective }}</p>
{% endcall %}

{# Section bar: SemiBold 18/28 #3a526d links (16/24 on phones), orange for the section in view and on hover, spread
   across the container from xl as in the frame. #}
<nav x-data="aboutSubnav" aria-label="Sections" class="sticky top-[var(--header-h,0px)] z-30 border-b border-outline bg-menu" data-figma="35098:39780">
  <div class="container-page">
    <ul x-ref="tabs" class="-mx-5 flex gap-6 overflow-x-auto px-5 [scrollbar-width:none] md:mx-0 md:gap-8 md:px-0 xl:justify-between xl:gap-4 [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden" data-figma="35098:39781">
      {% for s in t.sections %}
      <li class="shrink-0">
        <a href="#{{ s.id }}" data-section="{{ s.id }}" @click="go('{{ s.id }}')"
           :aria-current="active === '{{ s.id }}' ? 'location' : null"
           :class="active === '{{ s.id }}' ? 'text-accent' : 'text-card hover:text-accent'"
           class="block whitespace-nowrap py-4 text-base font-semibold transition-colors md:py-5 md:text-lg">{{ s.title }}</a>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</nav>

{# Search: right-aligned as in the frame (full width on phones, under it the result line). #}
<div x-data="termsSearch" class="container-page flex flex-col-reverse gap-3 pt-8 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between md:gap-6 md:pt-[50px]" data-figma="35098:39790">
  <p aria-live="polite" class="text-base text-body md:text-lg">
    <span x-show="needle" x-cloak>
      <span x-text="hits ? (hits === 1 ? '1 subsection mentions' : hits + ' subsections mention') + ' “' + q.trim() + '”.' : 'No subsection mentions “' + q.trim() + '”.'"></span>
      <button type="button" @click="clear()" class="link ml-2">Clear search</button>
    </span>
  </p>
  {{ searchField("Search Terms & Conditions", "Search the terms and conditions", "q", "go()") }}
</div>

{# The sections share one Back to Top button (the frame's "Back to Top" 35098:39814), sticky at the bottom right of the
   screen once a screen's height has been scrolled; after the last section it settles above the contact box. #}
<div class="relative" x-data="{ shown: false }" x-init="shown = scrollY > innerHeight" @scroll.window.throttle.100ms="shown = scrollY > innerHeight">
{% for s in t.sections %}
{% set tinted = loop.index0 % 2 == 1 %}
<section id="{{ s.id }}" data-term-section aria-labelledby="{{ s.id }}-title" class="{{ sectionOffset }} {{ 'bg-menu' if tinted else 'bg-white' }}" {% if s.figma %}data-figma="{{ s.figma }}"{% endif %}>
  <div class="container-page flex flex-col gap-6 py-8 md:gap-[30px] md:py-[50px]">
    {# Section Label: Medium 42/48 in the frame (here the repair pages' 24 / 32 / 40px title), 1px #3a526d rule. #}
    <div class="flex items-center gap-5 md:gap-9">
      <h2 id="{{ s.id }}-title" class="min-w-0 text-h3 font-medium text-heading md:text-h2 md:font-bold lg:text-h1">{{ s.title }}</h2>
      <span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px min-w-8 flex-1 bg-card"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="grid gap-8 xl:grid-cols-[minmax(0,756px)_300px] xl:justify-between">
      <div class="flex min-w-0 max-w-[756px] flex-col gap-8 md:gap-10">
        {% for it in s.items %}
        {# Subsection: the frame's "1.1  Title" (Regular 36/48) as a Medium 20/28 (24/32 from md) heading with the number
           hanging; text Regular 16/24 (18/28 from md) in the frame's navy, paragraphs 12px apart. #}
        <article id="{{ it.id }}" data-term aria-labelledby="{{ it.id }}-title" class="{{ itemOffset }} flex flex-col gap-3 md:gap-4" {% if it.figma %}data-figma="{{ it.figma }}"{% endif %}>
          <h3 id="{{ it.id }}-title" class="flex gap-3 text-h4 font-medium tracking-title text-heading md:text-h3"><span class="shrink-0">{{ it.num }}</span><span class="min-w-0">{{ it.title }}</span></h3>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 text-base text-primary-500 md:text-lg">
            {% for b in it.blocks %}{{ block(b, tinted) }}{% endfor %}
          </div>
        </article>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
      <nav aria-label="{{ s.title }} subsections" class="sticky top-[calc(var(--header-h,0px)_+_93px)] hidden self-start xl:block">
        <p class="text-base font-medium text-ink">In this section</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 flex flex-col border-l border-outline">
          {% for it in s.items %}
          <li data-term-link="{{ it.id }}">
            <a href="#{{ it.id }}" class="-ml-px flex gap-2 border-l-2 border-transparent py-1.5 pl-4 text-base text-primary-500 transition-colors hover:border-accent hover:text-accent"><span class="w-8 shrink-0 font-semibold">{{ it.num }}</span><span class="min-w-0">{{ it.short or it.title }}</span></a>
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}
{# White 52px button with the shadow of lifted cards; icon only on phones, where it sits over the text. #}
<div class="container-page pointer-events-none sticky bottom-5 z-20 flex justify-end md:bottom-8" data-figma="35098:39814">
  <a href="#top" x-show="shown" x-cloak x-transition.opacity aria-label="Back to Top"
     class="btn-secondary pointer-events-auto w-[52px] px-0 shadow-200 md:w-auto md:px-6">
    <span class="hidden md:inline">Back to Top</span>{% icon "dropdown-up", "h-6 w-6" %}
  </a>
</div>
</div>

{# Questions About These Terms? (the live page's closing box): the request strip's #eff7fd callout with the outline
   border, text on the left and the address and phone numbers on the right from md. #}
{% set ct = t.contact %}
<section class="bg-white" aria-labelledby="terms-contact-title">
  <div class="container-page pb-10 pt-6 md:pb-[50px] md:pt-8">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 rounded border border-outline bg-[#eff7fd] px-5 py-6 md:flex-row md:items-center md:justify-between md:gap-10 md:px-12 md:py-10">
      <div class="flex max-w-[593px] flex-col gap-2">
        <h2 id="terms-contact-title" class="text-h3 font-medium text-heading md:text-h2 md:font-bold">{{ ct.title }}</h2>
        <p class="text-base text-body md:text-lg">{{ ct.text }}</p>
      </div>
      <address class="flex shrink-0 flex-col gap-1 text-base not-italic text-ink md:text-lg">
        <span class="font-bold">{{ ct.company }}</span>
        <span>{{ ct.address | join("<br>") | safe }}</span>
        {% for ph in ct.phones %}
        <span class="{{ 'mt-2' if loop.first }}">{{ ph.label }}: <a href="{{ ph.href }}" class="link font-medium">{{ ph.number }}</a></span>
        {% endfor %}
      </address>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
